  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration of Migrants in Situations of Vulnerability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on over 40 years of assisted voluntary return and reintegration globally, IOM aims to enhance in Greece the assistance and the support provided to migrants in a situation of vulnerability, including migrants with health needs, victims of human trafficking, unaccompanied and separated children, who wish to return to their countries of origin or of habitual residence in safety and with dignity. Specifically, the project foresees to support 200 migrants in a situation of vulnerability with vulnerability screening and assessment, tailored assistance throughout the return continuum, and to contribute to their sustainable reintegration.</narrative>
  </description>
